      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habikino"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city earned the nickname Minami-Osaka, a nod to its location just south of Osaka city center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habikino"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ancient kofun burial mounds pepper Habikino, some dating back to the Kofun period and linked to early emperors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habikino"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Habikino’s history of yakiniku dates back about 140 years, making it a renowned meat‑cooking hub in Kansai.",
